... Respondent\(s\)

STATUTES & ACTS REFERRED:
Code of Criminal Procedure 1973, Bharatiya Nagarik Suraksha Sanhita 2023

SECTIONS & PROVISIONS:
CrPC Section 437\(5\), CrPC Section 439\(2\), BNSS Section 483\(3\)

KEY TOPICS & ISSUES:
Bail Cancellation, Supervening Circumstances, Tampering with Evidence, Personal Liberty, High Threshold

================================================================================
                                   JUDGMENT
================================================================================

1. FACTS OF THE CASE:
State sought cancellation of bail granted to political activist on grounds that he addressed public rallies criticizing the investigating agency.

2. ISSUES FRAMED:
What constitute valid legal grounds for cancelling bail under Section 439\(2\) CrPC / Section 483\(3\) BNSS?

3. LEGAL RATIO & FINDINGS:
Rejection of bail and cancellation of bail stand on entirely different legal footings; bail cannot be cancelled without cogent proof of witness tampering.

4. FINAL ORDER:
Criminal Appeal Dismissed; Bail cancellation refused; No evidence of witness tampering or misuse of liberty.

Ordered and decreed accordingly.

Hon'ble Justice B.R. Gavai & Justice Sandeep Mehta
Supreme Court of India
